{"id":"p08-l04","minutes":40,"summary":"The ideal low-pass filter’s impulse response is an infinite sinc. Truncate it and you get ripples; taper it with a window and you trade transition width for stopband depth. You design FIR filters with Hamming and Kaiser windows, size a Kaiser filter from a specification, and check the stopband meets it.","html":"<h2 id=\"the-ideal-filter-and-its-problem\">The ideal filter and its problem</h2>\n<p>An ideal low-pass with cutoff <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> (in cycles per sample) has the impulse response</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">sinc</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.113em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mop\">sin</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>which runs from <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span> to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">∞</span></span></span></span>. Keep <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> taps around the centre, shifted by <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span> so the filter is causal, and multiply by a <strong>window</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">d</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">n</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>The result is <strong>linear phase</strong>, with a delay of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span></span></span></span> samples, because <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">h</span></span></span></span> is symmetric.</p>\n<h2 id=\"windows\">Windows</h2>\n<p>Truncating abruptly (a rectangular window) leaves the Gibbs ripple: the first stopband sidelobe is only about −21 dB however many taps you use. Tapered windows push the sidelobes down at the cost of a wider transition:</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Window</th>\n<th>Stopband</th>\n<th>Transition width <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Rectangular</td>\n<td>−21 dB</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hamming</td>\n<td>−53 dB</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3.3/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Blackman</td>\n<td>−74 dB</td>\n<td><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5.5/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>The <strong>Kaiser window</strong> has a parameter β that tunes the trade-off continuously. For a stopband attenuation <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span></span></span></span> dB and a transition <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1102</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8.7</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\"> </span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">&gt;</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.2408em;vertical-align:-0.8804em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.3603em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2.285</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">⋅</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8804em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"firwin\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>A windowed-sinc low-pass with cutoff 0.1 f_s. The readout gives the worst level beyond 0.15 f_s; compare the windows and tap counts.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Specification: sample at 1 kHz; pass up to 100 Hz, attenuate by at least 60 dB above 150 Hz.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Transition: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">50/1000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05</span></span></span></span>. Design cutoff in the middle: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.1076em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">c</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.125</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Kaiser: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0528em;\">β</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.1102</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">60</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8.7</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5.65</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≈</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">52/</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2.285</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.05</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">73.4</span></span></span></span>, so 75 taps (odd, for a whole-sample delay).</li>\n<li>With the same 75 taps, a Hamming window reaches only about 56 dB at 150 Hz: its sidelobes level off in the 50s, so it can’t reliably meet 60 dB. Rectangular manages about 26 dB.</li>\n<li>Delay: 37 samples, 37 ms. Fine for logging, a lot for a control loop (lesson 7).</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">fir_window.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">from</span> scipy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> signal\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">fir_lowpass</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">n_taps, fc, window</span>):\n    m = (n_taps - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    k = np.arange(n_taps) - m\n    h = <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * fc * np.sinc(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * fc * k)                    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># np.sinc(x) = sin(pi x)/(pi x)</span>\n    h *= window\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> h / h.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">sum</span>()                                   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># unity gain at DC</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">hamming</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">n</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.54</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.46</span> * np.cos(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * np.arange(n) / (n - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">kaiser</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">n, beta</span>):\n    m = (n - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.i0(beta * np.sqrt(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - ((np.arange(n) - m) / m) ** <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>)) / np.i0(beta)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">kaiser_design</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">atten_db, df</span>):\n    beta = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.1102</span> * (atten_db - <span class=\"hljs-number\">8.7</span>) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> atten_db &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5842</span> * (atten_db - <span class=\"hljs-number\">21</span>) ** <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.4</span> + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.07886</span> * (atten_db - <span class=\"hljs-number\">21</span>)\n    n = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">int</span>(np.ceil((atten_db - <span class=\"hljs-number\">8</span>) / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2.285</span> * <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * np.pi * df) + <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)) | <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> n, beta\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">stopband_db</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">h, f_stop</span>):\n    w, H = signal.freqz(h, worN=<span class=\"hljs-number\">8192</span>, fs=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span> * np.log10(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(H[w &gt;= f_stop]).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>())\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">passband_ripple_db</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">h, f_pass</span>):\n    w, H = signal.freqz(h, worN=<span class=\"hljs-number\">8192</span>, fs=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>)\n    g = <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span> * np.log10(np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(H[w &lt;= f_pass]))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> g.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() - g.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>()\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    n, beta = kaiser_design(<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Kaiser design:&quot;</span>, n, <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;taps, beta&quot;</span>, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(beta, <span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> n == <span class=\"hljs-number\">75</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(beta - <span class=\"hljs-number\">5.653</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-3</span>\n    hk = fir_lowpass(n, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.125</span>, kaiser(n, beta))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(hk, signal.firwin(n, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.25</span>, window=(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;kaiser&quot;</span>, beta)), atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>)\n    sb, pr = stopband_db(hk, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.15</span>), passband_ripple_db(hk, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.10</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;Kaiser: stopband <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{sb:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> dB, passband ripple <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{pr:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> dB&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> sb &lt;= -<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> pr &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.02</span>\n    hh = fir_lowpass(n, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.125</span>, hamming(n))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(hh, signal.firwin(n, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.25</span>, window=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;hamming&quot;</span>), atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-12</span>)\n    ham = stopband_db(hh, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.15</span>)\n    rect = stopband_db(fir_lowpass(n, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.125</span>, np.ones(n)), <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.15</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;same 75 taps: Hamming <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{ham:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> dB, rectangular <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{rect:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> dB: neither meets 60 dB&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> -<span class=\"hljs-number\">60</span> &lt; ham &lt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">50</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> rect &gt; -<span class=\"hljs-number\">30</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(hk, hk[::-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>])                     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># symmetric: linear phase</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Halving the transition width at the same attenuation does what to the Kaiser filter length?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> is inversely proportional to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span>, so the length (and the delay, and the cost per sample) doubles.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why can’t a longer rectangular-window filter push its stopband below about −21 dB?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The Gibbs overshoot comes from the abrupt truncation, and its relative size doesn’t depend on <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span>. More taps make the transition narrower and the ripples squeeze toward the edge, but the first sidelobe stays near −21 dB.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p08-l04\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"the-ideal-filter-and-its-problem","title":"The ideal filter and its problem"},{"id":"windows","title":"Windows"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p08-l04-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Kaiser β for 60 dB attenuation?</p>\n","explain":"<p>0.1102(A − 8.7).</p>\n","answer":5.6533,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l04-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Estimated Kaiser length for 60 dB and Δf = 0.05 (before rounding)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(A − 8)/(2.285·2πΔf) + 1.</p>\n","answer":73.43,"tol":0.003,"unit":""},{"id":"p08-l04-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Group delay in samples of a 75-tap linear-phase FIR?</p>\n","explain":"<p>(N − 1)/2.</p>\n","answer":37,"tol":0.001,"unit":"samples"},{"id":"p08-l04-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>The Hamming window’s stopband is about…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Fixed, whatever N.</p>\n","options":["−53 dB","−74 dB","−21 dB","−120 dB"],"answer":0},{"id":"p08-l04-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>A symmetric FIR impulse response guarantees…</p>\n","explain":"<p>FIR is always stable; symmetry gives linear phase.</p>\n","options":["minimum phase","stability and linear phase","zero delay","an infinite stopband"],"answer":1},{"id":"p08-l04-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Design cutoff in cycles/sample for a 100–150 Hz transition at f_s = 1 kHz?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The middle of the transition.</p>\n","answer":0.125,"tol":0.001,"unit":""}],"code":[{"file":"fir_window.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\nfrom scipy import signal\n\ndef fir_lowpass(n_taps, fc, window):\n    m = (n_taps - 1) / 2\n    k = np.arange(n_taps) - m\n    h = 2 * fc * np.sinc(2 * fc * k)                    # np.sinc(x) = sin(pi x)/(pi x)\n    h *= window\n    return h / h.sum()                                   # unity gain at DC\n\ndef hamming(n):\n    return 0.54 - 0.46 * np.cos(2 * np.pi * np.arange(n) / (n - 1))\n\ndef kaiser(n, beta):\n    m = (n - 1) / 2\n    return np.i0(beta * np.sqrt(1 - ((np.arange(n) - m) / m) ** 2)) / np.i0(beta)\n\ndef kaiser_design(atten_db, df):\n    beta = 0.1102 * (atten_db - 8.7) if atten_db > 50 else 0.5842 * (atten_db - 21) ** 0.4 + 0.07886 * (atten_db - 21)\n    n = int(np.ceil((atten_db - 8) / (2.285 * 2 * np.pi * df) + 1)) | 1\n    return n, beta\n\ndef stopband_db(h, f_stop):\n    w, H = signal.freqz(h, worN=8192, fs=1.0)\n    return 20 * np.log10(np.abs(H[w >= f_stop]).max())\n\ndef passband_ripple_db(h, f_pass):\n    w, H = signal.freqz(h, worN=8192, fs=1.0)\n    g = 20 * np.log10(np.abs(H[w <= f_pass]))\n    return g.max() - g.min()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    n, beta = kaiser_design(60, 0.05)\n    print(\"Kaiser design:\", n, \"taps, beta\", round(beta, 3))\n    assert n == 75 and abs(beta - 5.653) < 1e-3\n    hk = fir_lowpass(n, 0.125, kaiser(n, beta))\n    assert np.allclose(hk, signal.firwin(n, 0.25, window=(\"kaiser\", beta)), atol=1e-12)\n    sb, pr = stopband_db(hk, 0.15), passband_ripple_db(hk, 0.10)\n    print(f\"Kaiser: stopband {sb:.1f} dB, passband ripple {pr:.3f} dB\")\n    assert sb <= -60 and pr < 0.02\n    hh = fir_lowpass(n, 0.125, hamming(n))\n    assert np.allclose(hh, signal.firwin(n, 0.25, window=\"hamming\"), atol=1e-12)\n    ham = stopband_db(hh, 0.15)\n    rect = stopband_db(fir_lowpass(n, 0.125, np.ones(n)), 0.15)\n    print(f\"same 75 taps: Hamming {ham:.1f} dB, rectangular {rect:.1f} dB: neither meets 60 dB\")\n    assert -60 < ham < -50 and rect > -30\n    assert np.allclose(hk, hk[::-1])                     # symmetric: linear phase"}]}